[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/174741267","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/1157#issuecomment-174741267","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1157","id":174741267,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3NDc0MTI2Nw==","user":{"login":"gvanrossum","id":2894642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTQ2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2894642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum","html_url":"https://github.com/gvanrossum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-26T00:18:30Z","updated_at":"2016-01-26T00:18:30Z","body":"So this seems a bug in parsing lambda args. Note that `lambda (x, y): ...` is not the same as `lambda x, y: ...` -- the former is a tuple argument of length 2.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/174741267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gvanrossum","id":2894642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTQ2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2894642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum","html_url":"https://github.com/gvanrossum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/174741329","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/1157#issuecomment-174741329","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1157","id":174741329,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3NDc0MTMyOQ==","user":{"login":"gnprice","id":28173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice","html_url":"https://github.com/gnprice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-26T00:18:39Z","updated_at":"2016-01-26T00:18:39Z","body":"I think the issue here is that\n- the `FuncExpr` code is assuming that the body of a lambda is always one statement, a return statement:\n\n```\n    def expr(self) -> Node:\n        \"\"\"Return the expression (the body) of the lambda.\"\"\"\n        ret = cast(ReturnStmt, self.body.body[0])\n        return ret.expr\n```\n- The way we handled #934, in PR #929, made that not true when we have a Python 2 tuple-parameter to desugar -- the body can start instead with an AssignmentStmt. See in particular here: https://github.com/jukkal/mypy/blob/master/mypy/nodes.py#L291\n\nProbably the immediate fix is to complicate `FuncExpr.expr` to handle this case -- maybe just change `body[0]` to `body[-1]`? That'll still feel a little awkward and potentially fragile. But it's probably OK in practice because we're not likely to add more desugaring like #929 -- we believe we're done parsing all syntax.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/174741329/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gnprice","id":28173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice","html_url":"https://github.com/gnprice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/events{/privacy}","received_events